  "reason": "Offline export removal (instruments-single-source e2e91b11; owner decision in acceptance-reports/instruments-research-2026-11-27/PLAN.md \"Owner decisions on single-source.md\"; hand record, no --bless). The OfflineAudioContext export path has no production caller: rg for renderMixdown, renderStemMixdown, createStemRenderSession, createOfflineMixerNodes, offline-instrument-renderers and apply-offline-routing over every .ts, .tsx and .json file outside tools/certification finds no match at this commit; production export runs the portable export worker and the native export plan. A whole-file deletion is not admissible through --allow-removal, so the engine gates leave their `files` maps as whole-object changes (diffJson records a removed key as old -> null, which setAt cannot apply) after the one-field export-mixdown change. Direct audit of every removed test. (1) export-mixdown.test.ts 'runtime-only cue routing > is explicitly rejected by offline export': asserted that renderMixdown rejects cueTrackIds with 'Cue routing is live-only and cannot be exported.'; renderMixdown is deleted and nothing else calls it, so the rejection path does not exist. Cue routing itself stays covered by mixer/cue-routing.test.ts (1 pass, unchanged). (2) export-mixdown.test.ts 'offline instrument scheduling > does not fabricate a synth for instrument tracks without a persisted device': drove renderMixdown through a fake OfflineAudioContext and counted oscillators; offline-instrument-renderers.ts and the renderMixdown instrument scheduling are deleted, so no offline path can fabricate a synth. Verified: bun test of export-mixdown.test.ts on this branch runs 19 pass, 0 fail (pinned 21). (3) mixer/apply-offline-routing.test.ts (4 tests: 'wraps registration and construction rejection with processor context', 'rejects runtime faults instead of silently succeeding', 'turns malformed processor messages into protocol faults', 'cleans up an earlier processor when a later sequential construction rejects'): the compressor failure contract of createOfflineMixerNodes in apply-offline-routing.ts, both deleted; the file imported ./offline-compressor-lifecycle, which this branch still contains but no .ts or .tsx file imports (rg finds no importer), so those four tests exercised only the deleted offline graph builder. Live routing keeps mixer/apply-live-routing.test.ts (4 pass, unchanged). (4) portable-export-legacy-comparison.browser.test.ts (1 test, 'the portable export worker matches the legacy OfflineAudioContext render'): compared the portable worker against a legacy OfflineAudioContext render (automation worst diff < 0.5 dB, sidechain < 3.5 dB outside key edges); with the legacy renderer deleted there is nothing to compare against, and the portable path keeps portable-export-worker.test.ts (6), portable-export-automation.test.ts (8) and export-fidelity.test.ts (8), unchanged. No killer is removed: none of the seven tests is named in an arm's expect.fails or a gate's judge.fails. Counts: f-engine and last-engine files: export-mixdown.test.ts pass 21 -> 19, apply-offline-routing.test.ts (pass 4) and portable-export-legacy-comparison.browser.test.ts (pass 1) removed. The engine judge pins per-file counts only; no aggregate count in any gate includes them. removals/instruments-single-source.json and .md are deleted: this record supersedes them.",
